Kinogaki FBX reader

The code of this repository is original. It was written with two open-source
FBX readers open as references for how the format behaves; no code was copied
from either, and neither is a dependency:

- ufbx, https://github.com/ufbx/ufbx, Copyright (c) 2020 Samuli Raivio,
  MIT License or public domain (Unlicense).
- assimp, https://github.com/assimp/assimp, Copyright (c) 2006-2026 assimp
  team, BSD 3-Clause License.

These parts follow ufbx closely, as facts about files rather than code:

- The families of materials (src/fbx/scene/shading.rs, `family`): Maya's
  shader `RenderAPI` names (ARNOLD_SHADER_ID, OSL, SFX_PBS_SHADER), the
  3ds Max class IDs of the Physical, PBR, glTF and OpenPBR materials, and
  the order the three are asked in.
- Which property templates apply to which objects
  (src/fbx/scene/graph.rs, `Graph::template`).
- The meaning of `InheritType` and how a child inherits its parent's scale
  under each (src/fbx/scene/transform.rs, `Placed`).

The order of the transform stack is the one Autodesk's FBX SDK documents.
